    "created_at": "2021-03-11T04:18:08Z",
    "updated_at": "2021-03-18T02:35:13Z",
    "body": ">  I sure hope no implementations are ignoring integrity.\r\n\r\n🤣😭 ... you see where I'm going with this. But yeah, I'm pretty sure they do across most, if not all, UAs for web manifest at least. Not sure about icons. This was my primary motivation for moving link type manifest to the HTML spec. The other general problem is things like CSP being ignored for linked sub-resources. \r\n\r\nThis is why I'd like to see a unified/generalized attribute processing model for link relationships. Lots of things are getting ignored and I'm worried it's going to come back to bite us.  \r\n\r\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
