    "created_at": "2021-03-17T09:13:39Z",
    "updated_at": "2021-03-17T09:13:39Z",
    "body": "I really like the idea of ensuring that when HTML link types agree on an attribute the processing model is consistent.\r\n\r\nI think in principle HTML link types should opt-in to additional attributes and not opt-out. `crossorigin`/`integrity`/`referrerpolicy` are special cases as they pertain to fetching itself and not selection of a link (and even these are not quite the same, e.g., `crossorigin`/`integrity` only apply to external resources, not hyperlinks).",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
    "reactions": {
